{"name":"Pulled Taffy","hex":"#f1d6bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pulled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of pull"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of cooked meat, prepared by being torn into fine pieces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pulled"},{"term":"taffy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, chewy candy made from boiled sugar, molasses, or corn syrup and butter.","Flattery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taffy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taffy (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Taffy is a type of candy invented in the United States, made by stretching or pulling a sticky mass of a soft candy base, made of boiled sugar, butter, vegetable oil, flavorings, and colorings, until it becomes aerated, resulting in a light, fluffy and chewy candy. When this process is complete, the taffy is rolled, cut into small pieces and wrapped in wax paper to keep it soft. It is usually pastel-colored and fruit-flavored, but other flavors are common as well, including molasses and the \"classic\" (unflavored) taffy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/330px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffy_(candy)","wikidata":"Q7892214"},{"title":"Taffy (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Taffy\" is a song written and sung by Lisa Loeb. The song was recorded in 1995. It is featured on her album Tails, and her 2006 greatest hits album, The Very Best of Lisa Loeb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fc/Lisa_Loeb_Taffy.jpeg/330px-Lisa_Loeb_Taffy.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffy_(song)","wikidata":"Q7674960"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-